{"repositoryId":879072703,"availability":"available","full":"sister-software/mailwoman","name":"mailwoman","description":"Postal address intelligence for parsing, geocoding, and matching.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":5,"forks":1,"created":"2024-10-26T22:26:18Z","updated":"2026-10-18T06:46:11Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://mailwoman.ai/","topics":["address","address-validation","geocoder","geocoding","onnx","postal","spatial-analysis"],"demo":"https://mailwoman.ai/demo","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:57.038Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:57.038Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:57.038Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T07:12:57.038Z","stars":5,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A calibrated, retrieval-augmented postal-address parser.","Mailwoman turns free-text postal addresses into structured components (house number, street, locality, region, postcode, country) and resolves them to coordinates against an open gazetteer. It is a small transformer encoder (30M params) that performs BIO token classification over a 33-label schema. It is not an LLM, and no part of it is generative. It performs conventional entity recognition. That method suits short, structured strings.","It runs in Node.js and the browser, without Elasticsearch or a multi-gigabyte libpostal install. The model is about 30 MB. It resolves coordinates from a SQLite gazetteer at the finest tier available: admin, postcode, street, or rooftop (US and French national registers)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sister-software/mailwoman/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b4e62534e625522ae1468fb1d40dffdfb45cc6dce84ece8e81d89de056ebe127","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:57.118Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:57.118Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A calibrated, retrieval-augmented postal-address parser.","sourceUrl":"htt